<section itemprop=3D"content"><h1 class=3D"r2022a" itemprop=3D"title conten=
t" id=3D"example-ex52066105">Classify Defects on Wafer Maps Using Deep Lear=
ning</h1><div class=3D"examples_short_list hidden_ios_android"><div data-pa=
ne=3D"metadata" class=3D"panel metadata_container panel-default"><div class=
=3D"panel-body metadata_content open_example_div"><button class=3D"btn btn_=
color_blue btn-block add_margin_10 analyticsOpenWith">Try This Example</but=
ton><p class=3D"add_margin_5">This example uses:</p><ul class=3D"list-unsty=
led add_border_bottom example_product_list" itemprop=3D"requiredprods"><li>=
<a class=3D"coming_from_product" href=3D"matlab:matlab.internal.language.in=
trospective.showAddon('IP')">Image Processing Toolbox</a><a class=3D"not_co=
ming_from_product" href=3D"https://www.mathworks.com/help/images/index.html=
">Image Processing Toolbox</a></li><li><a class=3D"coming_from_product" hre=
f=3D"matlab:matlab.internal.language.introspective.showAddon('NN')">Deep Le=
arning Toolbox</a><a class=3D"not_coming_from_product" href=3D"https://www.=
mathworks.com/help/deeplearning/index.html">Deep Learning Toolbox</a></li><=
li><a class=3D"coming_from_product" href=3D"matlab:matlab.internal.language=
.introspective.showAddon('ST')">Statistics and Machine Learning Toolbox</a>=
<a class=3D"not_coming_from_product" href=3D"https://www.mathworks.com/help=
/stats/index.html">Statistics and Machine Learning Toolbox</a></li></ul><bu=
tton type=3D"button" class=3D"btn companion_btn btn_color_blue btn-block co=
py_cmd_btn" data-toggle=3D"popover" data-placement=3D"bottom" data-trigger=
=3D"hover focus" title=3D"" data-html=3D"true" data-content=3D"<code>openEx=
ample('images_deeplearning/ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample'=
)</code>" data-original-title=3D"MATLAB Command">Copy Command &nbsp;<span c=
lass=3D"icon-mw-copy"><span class=3D"sr-only">Copy Code</span></span></butt=
on></div></div></div><div itemscope=3D"" itemtype=3D"http://www.mathworks.c=
om/help/schema/MathWorksDocPage/Example" itemprop=3D"example" class=3D"em_e=
xample"><meta itemprop=3D"exampleid" content=3D"images_deeplearning-Classif=
yWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample"><meta itemprop=3D"exampletitle" c=
ontent=3D"Classify Defects on Wafer Maps Using Deep Learning"></div><span i=
d=3D"ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample" class=3D"anchor_targe=
t"></span><p class=3D"shortdesc">This example shows how to classify eight t=
ypes of manufacturing defects on wafer maps using a simple convolutional ne=
ural network (CNN).</p><p>Wafers are thin disks of semiconducting material,=
 typically silicon, that serve as the foundation for integrated circuits. E=
ach wafer yields several individual circuits (ICs), separated into dies. Au=
tomated inspection machines test the performance of ICs on the wafer. The m=
achines produce images, called wafer maps, that indicate which dies perform=
 correctly (pass) and which dies do not meet performance standards (fail).<=
/p><p>The spatial pattern of the passing and failing dies on a wafer map ca=
n indicate specific issues in the manufacturing process. Deep learning appr=
oaches can efficiently classify the defect pattern on a large number of waf=
ers. Therefore, by using deep learning, you can quickly identify manufactur=
ing issues, enabling prompt repair of the manufacturing process and reducin=
g waste.</p><p>This example shows how to train a classification network tha=
t detects and classifies eight types of manufacturing defect patterns. The =
example also shows how to evaluate the performance of the network.</p><div =
class=3D"procedure"><h3 class=3D"title" id=3D"ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingD=
eepLearningExample-1">Download WM-811K Wafer Defect Map Data<span id=3D"mw_=
rtc_ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample_T_597CCCEE" class=3D"an=
chor_target"></span></h3><p>This example uses the WM-811K Wafer Defect Map =
data set [<a href=3D"https://www.mathworks.com/help/images/classify-anomali=
es-on-wafer-defect-maps-using-deep-learning.html#mw_rtc_ClassifyWaferMapDef=
ectsUsingDeepLearningExample_M_F263539E" class=3D"intrnllnk">1</a>] [<a hre=
f=3D"https://www.mathworks.com/help/images/classify-anomalies-on-wafer-defe=
ct-maps-using-deep-learning.html#mw_rtc_ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLea=
rningExample_M_F3BDC10F" class=3D"intrnllnk">2</a>]. The data set consists =
of 811,457 wafer maps images, including 172,950 labeled images. Each image =
has only three pixel values. The value <code class=3D"literal">0</code> ind=
icates the background, the value <code class=3D"literal">1</code> represent=
s correctly behaving dies, and the value <code class=3D"literal">2</code> r=
epresents defective dies. The labeled images have one of nine labels based =
on the spatial pattern of the defective dies. The size of the data set is 3=
.5 GB.</p><p>Set <code class=3D"literal">dataDir</code> as the desired loca=
tion of the data set. Download the data set using the <code class=3D"litera=
l">downloadWaferMapData</code> helper function. This function is attached t=
o the example as a supporting file.</p><div class=3D"code_responsive"><div =
class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>dataDir =3D fullfile=
(tempdir,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"WaferDefects"</span>);
downloadWaferMapData(dataDir)</pre></div></div></div><h3 class=3D"title" id=
=3D"ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample-2">Preprocess and Augme=
nt Data</h3><p>The data is stored in a MAT file as an array of structures. =
Load the data set into the workspace.</p><div class=3D"code_responsive"><di=
v class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>dataMatFile =3D fu=
llfile(dataDir,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"MIR-WM811K"</span>,<span styl=
e=3D"color:#A020F0">"WM811K.mat"</span>);
waferData =3D load(dataMatFile);
waferData =3D waferData.data;</pre></div></div></div><p>Explore the data by=
 displaying the first element of the structure. The <code class=3D"literal"=
>waferMap</code> field contains the image data. The <code class=3D"literal"=
>failureType</code> field contains the label of the defect.</p><div class=
=3D"code_responsive"><div class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"=
><pre>disp(waferData(1))</pre></div></div></div><div class=3D"code_responsi=
ve"><div class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeoutput"><pre>          =
waferMap: [45=C3=9748 uint8]
           dieSize: 1683
           lotName: 'lot1'
        waferIndex: 1
    trainTestLabel: 'Training'
       failureType: 'none'
</pre></div></div></div><h4 class=3D"title" id=3D"ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUs=
ingDeepLearningExample-3">Reformat Data</h4><p>This example uses only label=
ed images. Remove the unlabeled images from the structure.</p><div class=3D=
"code_responsive"><div class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><p=
re>unlabeledImages =3D zeros(size(waferData),<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">=
"logical"</span>);
<span style=3D"color:#0000FF">for</span> idx =3D 1:size(unlabeledImages,1)
    unlabeledImages(idx) =3D isempty(waferData(idx).trainTestLabel);
<span style=3D"color:#0000FF">end</span>
waferData(unlabeledImages) =3D [];</pre></div></div></div><p>The <code clas=
s=3D"literal">dieSize</code>, <code class=3D"literal">lotName</code>, and <=
code class=3D"literal">waferIndex</code> fields are not relevant to the cla=
ssification of the images. The example partitions data into training, valid=
ation, and test sets using a different convention than specified by <code c=
lass=3D"literal">trainTestLabel</code> field. Remove these fields from the =
structure using the <a href=3D"https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/ref/rm=
field.html" data-docid=3D"matlab_ref#btt32r0" class=3D"a"><code class=3D"ol=
ink">rmfield</code></a> function.</p><div class=3D"code_responsive"><div cl=
ass=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>fieldsToRemove =3D [<s=
pan style=3D"color:#A020F0">"dieSize"</span>,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">=
"lotName"</span>,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"waferIndex"</span>,<span st=
yle=3D"color:#A020F0">"trainTestLabel"</span>];
waferData =3D rmfield(waferData,fieldsToRemove);</pre></div></div></div><p>=
Specify the image classes.</p><div class=3D"code_responsive"><div class=3D"=
programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>defectClasses =3D [<span styl=
e=3D"color:#A020F0">"Center"</span>,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"Donut"</=
span>,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"Edge-Loc"</span>,<span style=3D"color:=
#A020F0">"Edge-Ring"</span>,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"Loc"</span>,<spa=
n style=3D"color:#A020F0">"Near-full"</span>,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">=
"Random"</span>,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"Scratch"</span>,<span style=
=3D"color:#A020F0">"none"</span>];
numClasses =3D numel(defectClasses);</pre></div></div></div><p>To apply add=
itional preprocessing operations on the data, such as resizing the image to=
 match the network input size or applying random train the network for clas=
sification, you can use an augmented image datastore. You cannot create an =
augmented image datastore from data in a structure, but you can create the =
datastore from data in a table. Convert the data into a table with two vari=
ables:</p><div class=3D"itemizedlist"><ul><li><p><code class=3D"literal">Wa=
ferImage</code> - Wafer defect map images</p></li><li><p><code class=3D"lit=
eral">FailureType</code> - Categorical label for each image</p></li></ul></=
div><div class=3D"code_responsive"><div class=3D"programlisting"><div class=
=3D"codeinput"><pre>waferData =3D struct2table(waferData);
waferData.Properties.VariableNames =3D [<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"Wafe=
rImage"</span>,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"FailureType"</span>];
waferData.FailureType =3D categorical(waferData.FailureType,defectClasses);=
</pre></div></div></div><p>Display a sample image from each input image cla=
ss using the <code class=3D"literal">displaySampleWaferMaps</code> helper f=
unction. This function is attached to the example as a supporting file.</p>=
<div class=3D"code_responsive"><div class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"=
codeinput"><pre>displaySampleWaferMaps(waferData)</pre></div></div></div><d=
iv class=3D"informalfigure"><div id=3D"d123e52197" class=3D"mediaobject"><p=
><img src=3D"https://www.mathworks.com/help/examples/images_deeplearning/wi=
n64/ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample_01.png" width=3D"560"><=
/p></div></div><h4 class=3D"title" id=3D"ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLe=
arningExample-4">Balance Data By Oversampling<span id=3D"mw_rtc_ClassifyWaf=
erMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample_T_9D564B93" class=3D"anchor_target"></=
span></h4><p>Display the number of images of each class. The data set is he=
avily unbalanced, with significantly fewer images of each defect class than=
 the number of images without defects. </p><div class=3D"code_responsive"><=
div class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>summary(waferDat=
a.FailureType)</pre></div></div></div><div class=3D"code_responsive"><div c=
lass=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeoutput"><pre>     Center         =
  4294=20
     Donut             555=20
     Edge-Loc         5189=20
     Edge-Ring        9680=20
     Loc              3593=20
     Near-full         149=20
     Random            866=20
     Scratch          1193=20
     none           147431=20
</pre></div></div></div><p>To improve the class balancing, oversample the d=
efect classes using the <code class=3D"literal">oversampleWaferDefectClasse=
s</code> helper function. This function is attached to the example as a sup=
porting file. The helper function appends the data set with five modified c=
opies of each defect image. Each copy has one of these modifications: horiz=
ontal reflection, vertical reflection, or rotation by a multiple of 90 degr=
ees.</p><div class=3D"code_responsive"><div class=3D"programlisting"><div c=
lass=3D"codeinput"><pre>waferData =3D oversampleWaferDefectClasses(waferDat=
a);</pre></div></div></div><p>Display the number of images of each class af=
ter class balancing.</p><div class=3D"code_responsive"><div class=3D"progra=
mlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>summary(waferData.FailureType)</pre=
></div></div></div><div class=3D"code_responsive"><div class=3D"programlist=
ing"><div class=3D"codeoutput"><pre>     Center          25764=20
     Donut            3330=20
     Edge-Loc        31134=20
     Edge-Ring       58080=20
     Loc             21558=20
     Near-full         894=20
     Random           5196=20
     Scratch          7158=20
     none           147431=20
</pre></div></div></div><h4 class=3D"title" id=3D"ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUs=
ingDeepLearningExample-5">Partition Data into Training, Validation, and Tes=
t Sets<span id=3D"mw_rtc_ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample_T_=
46B58721" class=3D"anchor_target"></span></h4><p>Split the oversampled data=
 set into training, validation, and test sets using the <a href=3D"https://=
www.mathworks.com/help/vision/ref/splitlabels.html" data-docid=3D"vision_re=
f#mw_c3ecb099-70f0-4ea2-923c-d66fdc4beadb" class=3D"a"><code class=3D"olink=
">splitlabels</code></a><span role=3D"cross_prod"> (Computer Vision Toolbox=
)</span> function. Approximately 90% of the data is used for training, 5% i=
s used for validation, and 5% is used for testing.</p><div class=3D"code_re=
sponsive"><div class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>label=
Idx =3D splitlabels(waferData,[0.9 0.05 0.05],<span style=3D"color:#A020F0"=
>"randomized"</span>,TableVariable=3D<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"Failure=
Type"</span>);
trainingData =3D waferData(labelIdx{1},:);
validationData =3D waferData(labelIdx{2},:);
testingData =3D waferData(labelIdx{3},:);</pre></div></div></div><h4 class=
=3D"title" id=3D"ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample-6">Augment=
 Training Data</h4><p>Specify a set of random augmentations to apply to the=
 training data using an <a href=3D"https://www.mathworks.com/help/deeplearn=
ing/ref/imagedataaugmenter.html" data-docid=3D"nnet_ref#mw_bb6aac9c-0a3d-47=
00-b4f9-82088d9ad021" class=3D"a"><code class=3D"olink">imageDataAugmenter<=
/code></a><span role=3D"cross_prod"> (Deep Learning Toolbox)</span> object.=
 Adding random augmentations to the training images can avoid the network f=
rom overfitting to the training data. </p><div class=3D"code_responsive"><d=
iv class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>aug =3D imageData=
Augmenter(FillValue=3D0,RandXReflection=3Dtrue,RandYReflection=3Dtrue,RandR=
otation=3D[0 360]);</pre></div></div></div><p>Specify the input size for th=
e network. Create an <a href=3D"https://www.mathworks.com/help/deeplearning=
/ref/augmentedimagedatastore.html" data-docid=3D"nnet_ref#mw_fd462475-1bc2-=
4f76-968c-c75721e5195f" class=3D"a"><code class=3D"olink">augmentedImageDat=
astore</code></a><span role=3D"cross_prod"> (Deep Learning Toolbox)</span> =
that reads the training data, resizes the data to the network input size, a=
nd applies random augmentations.</p><div class=3D"code_responsive"><div cla=
ss=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>inputSize =3D [48 48];
dsTrain =3D augmentedImageDatastore(inputSize,trainingData,<span style=3D"c=
olor:#A020F0">"FailureType"</span>,DataAugmentation=3Daug);</pre></div></di=
v></div><p>Create datastores that read validation and test data and resize =
the data to the network input size. You do not need to apply random augment=
ations to validation or test data.</p><div class=3D"code_responsive"><div c=
lass=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>dsVal =3D augmentedIm=
ageDatastore(inputSize,validationData,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"Failur=
eType"</span>);
dsVal.MiniBatchSize =3D 64;
dsTest =3D augmentedImageDatastore(inputSize,testingData,<span style=3D"col=
or:#A020F0">"FailureType"</span>);</pre></div></div></div><h3 class=3D"titl=
e" id=3D"ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample-7">Create Network<=
span id=3D"mw_rtc_ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample_T_DCCF575=
5" class=3D"anchor_target"></span></h3><p>Define the convolutional neural n=
etwork architecture. The range of the image input layer reflects the fact t=
hat the wafer maps have only three levels.</p><div class=3D"code_responsive=
"><div class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>layers =3D [
    imageInputLayer([inputSize 1], <span style=3D"color:#0000FF">...</span>
        Normalization=3D<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"rescale-zero-one"</s=
pan>,Min=3D0,Max=3D2);
   =20
    convolution2dLayer(3,8,Padding=3D<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"same"</=
span>)
    batchNormalizationLayer
    reluLayer
   =20
    maxPooling2dLayer(2,Stride=3D2)=20

    convolution2dLayer(3,16,Padding=3D<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"same"<=
/span>)=20
    batchNormalizationLayer
    reluLayer
   =20
    maxPooling2dLayer(2,Stride=3D2)=20
   =20
    convolution2dLayer(3,32,Padding=3D<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"same"<=
/span>)=20
    batchNormalizationLayer
    reluLayer

    maxPooling2dLayer(2,Stride=3D2)=20
   =20
    convolution2dLayer(3,64,Padding=3D<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"same"<=
/span>)=20
    batchNormalizationLayer
    reluLayer
   =20
    dropoutLayer

    fullyConnectedLayer(numClasses)
    softmaxLayer
    classificationLayer];</pre></div></div></div><h3 class=3D"title" id=3D"=
ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample-8">Specify Training Options=
<span id=3D"mw_rtc_ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample_H_E04718=
6C" class=3D"anchor_target"></span></h3><p>Specify the training options for=
 Adam optimization. Train the network for 30 epochs.</p><div class=3D"code_=
responsive"><div class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>opt=
ions =3D trainingOptions(<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"adam"</span>, <span=
 style=3D"color:#0000FF">...</span>
    ResetInputNormalization=3Dtrue, <span style=3D"color:#0000FF">...</span=
><span style=3D"color:#228B22"> </span>
    MaxEpochs=3D30, <span style=3D"color:#0000FF">...</span>
    InitialLearnRate=3D0.001, <span style=3D"color:#0000FF">...</span>
    L2Regularization=3D0.001, <span style=3D"color:#0000FF">...</span>
    MiniBatchSize=3D64, <span style=3D"color:#0000FF">...</span>
    Shuffle=3D<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"every-epoch"</span>, <span sty=
le=3D"color:#0000FF">...</span>
    Verbose=3Dfalse, <span style=3D"color:#0000FF">...</span>
    Plots=3D<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"training-progress"</span>, <span=
 style=3D"color:#0000FF">...</span>
    ValidationData=3DdsVal, <span style=3D"color:#0000FF">...</span>
    ValidationFrequency=3D20);</pre></div></div></div><h3 class=3D"title" i=
d=3D"ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample-9">Train Network or Do=
wnload Pretrained Network<span id=3D"mw_rtc_ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDee=
pLearningExample_T_AE592A8C" class=3D"anchor_target"></span></h3><p>By defa=
ult, the example loads a pretrained wafer defect classification network. Th=
e pretrained network enables you to run the entire example without waiting =
for training to complete.</p><p>To train the network, set the <code class=
=3D"literal">doTraining</code> variable in the following code to <code clas=
s=3D"literal">true</code>. Train the model using the <a href=3D"https://www=
.mathworks.com/help/deeplearning/ref/trainnetwork.html" data-docid=3D"nnet_=
ref#bu6sn4c" class=3D"a"><code class=3D"olink">trainNetwork</code></a><span=
 role=3D"cross_prod"> (Deep Learning Toolbox)</span> function.</p><p>Train =
on a GPU if one is available. Using a GPU requires Parallel Computing Toolb=
ox=E2=84=A2 and a CUDA=C2=AE enabled NVIDIA=C2=AE GPU. For more information=
, see <a href=3D"https://www.mathworks.com/help/parallel-computing/gpu-supp=
ort-by-release.html" data-docid=3D"distcomp_ug#mw_57e04559-0b60-42d5-ad55-e=
77ec5f5865f" class=3D"a">GPU Support by Release</a><span role=3D"cross_prod=
"> (Parallel Computing Toolbox)</span>.</p><div class=3D"code_responsive"><=
div class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>doTraining =3D <=
span class=3D"live_control_container"><img tabindex=3D"-1" alt=3D"" src=3D"=
https://www.mathworks.com/help/examples/images_deeplearning/win64/ClassifyW=
aferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample_09.png"><span data-examplename=3D"op=
enExample('images_deeplearning/ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExam=
ple')" tabindex=3D"0" data-controlvalue=3D"false" data-trigger=3D"focus" da=
ta-container=3D"body" data-toggle=3D"popover" data-placement=3D"top" data-h=
tml=3D"true" class=3D"popover_trigger add_cursor_pointer live_control_equiv=
alent_value" data-original-title=3D"" title=3D"">false</span></span>;
<span style=3D"color:#0000FF">if</span> doTraining
    trainedNet =3D trainNetwork(dsTrain,layers,options);
    modelDateTime =3D string(datetime(<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"now"</=
span>,Format=3D<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"yyyy-MM-dd-HH-mm-ss"</span>))=
;
    save(fullfile(dataDir,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"trained-WM811K-"</=
span>+modelDateTime+<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">".mat"</span>),<span styl=
e=3D"color:#A020F0">"trainedNet"</span>);

<span style=3D"color:#0000FF">else</span>
    downloadTrainedWaferNet(dataDir);
    trainedNet =3D load(fullfile(dataDir,<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"CNN=
-WM811K.mat"</span>));
    trainedNet =3D trainedNet.preTrainedNetwork;
<span style=3D"color:#0000FF">end</span></pre></div></div></div><h3 class=
=3D"title" id=3D"ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLearningExample-10">Quanti=
fy Network Performance on Test Data</h3><p>Classify each of test image usin=
g the <a href=3D"https://www.mathworks.com/help/deeplearning/ref/seriesnetw=
