</pre></div></div></div><h4 class=3D"title" id=3D"ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUs=
ingDeepLearningExample-12">Precision-Recall Curves and Area-Under-Curve (AU=
C)</h4><p>In addition to returning a classification of each test image, the=
 network can also predict the probability that a test image is each of the =
defect classes. In this case, precision-recall curves provide an alternativ=
e way to evaluate the network performance.</p><p>To calculate precision-rec=
all curves, start by performing a binary classification for each defect cla=
ss by comparing the probability against an arbitrary threshold. When the pr=
obability exceeds the threshold, you can assign the image to the target cla=
ss. The choice of threshold impacts the number of TP, FP, and FN results an=
d the precision and recall scores. To evaluate the network performance, you=
 must consider the performance at a range of thresholds. Precision-recall c=
urves plot the tradeoff between precision and recall values as you adjust t=
he threshold for the binary classification. The AUC metric summarizes the p=
recision-recall curve for a class as a single number in the range [0, 1], w=
here 1 indicates a perfect classification regardless of threshold.</p><p>Ca=
lculate the probability that each test image belongs to each of the defect =
classes using the <a href=3D"https://www.mathworks.com/help/deeplearning/re=
f/seriesnetwork.predict.html" data-docid=3D"nnet_ref#mw_0a51db93-cccf-4b2f-=
ae4c-6724cbf5ec46" class=3D"a"><code class=3D"olink">predict</code></a><spa=
n role=3D"cross_prod"> (Deep Learning Toolbox)</span> function.</p><div cla=
ss=3D"code_responsive"><div class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinpu=
t"><pre>defectProbabilities =3D predict(trainedNet,dsTest);</pre></div></di=
v></div><p>Use the <code class=3D"literal">rocmetrics</code> function to ca=
lculate the precision, recall, and AUC for each class over a range of thres=
holds. Plot the precision-recall curves.</p><div class=3D"code_responsive">=
<div class=3D"programlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>roc =3D rocmetr=
ics(defectTruth,defectProbabilities,defectClasses,AdditionalMetrics=3D<span=
 style=3D"color:#A020F0">"prec"</span>);
figure
plot(roc,XAxisMetric=3D<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"reca"</span>,YAxisMet=
ric=3D<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"prec"</span>);
xlabel(<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"Recall"</span>)
ylabel(<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"Precision"</span>)
grid <span style=3D"color:#A020F0">on</span>
title(<span style=3D"color:#A020F0">"Precision-Recall Curves for All Classe=
s"</span>)</pre></div></div></div><div class=3D"informalfigure"><div id=3D"=
d123e52414" class=3D"mediaobject"><p><img src=3D"https://www.mathworks.com/=
help/examples/images_deeplearning/win64/ClassifyWaferMapDefectsUsingDeepLea=
rningExample_03.png" width=3D"560"></p></div></div><p>The precision-recall =
curve for an ideal classifier passes through the point (1, 1). The classes =
that have precision-recall curves that tend towards (1, 1), such as <code c=
lass=3D"literal">Edge-Ring</code> and <code class=3D"literal">Center</code>=
, are the classes for which the network has the best performance. The netwo=
rk has the worst performance for the <code class=3D"literal">Scratch</code>=
 class.</p><p>Compute and display the AUC values of the precision/recall cu=
rves for each class.</p><div class=3D"code_responsive"><div class=3D"progra=
mlisting"><div class=3D"codeinput"><pre>prAUC =3D zeros(numClasses, 1);
<span style=3D"color:#0000FF">for</span> idx =3D 1:numClasses
    defectClass =3D defectClasses(idx);
    currClassIdx =3D strcmpi(roc.Metrics.ClassName, defectClass);
    reca =3D roc.Metrics.TruePositiveRate(currClassIdx);
    prec =3D roc.Metrics.PositivePredictiveValue(currClassIdx);
    prAUC(idx) =3D trapz(reca(2:end),prec(2:end)); <span style=3D"color:#22=
8B22">% prec(1) is always NaN</span>
<span style=3D"color:#0000FF">end</span>
prTable.AUC =3D prAUC;
prTable</pre></div></div></div><div class=3D"code_responsive"><div class=3D=
